  "step_3": "The decision reason requires focusing on the probability of the maximum outcome and preferring the one with the lower such probability. While the individual does mention the 80% probability (which is relevant to Lottery B’s maximum outcome), they do not compare it to the 100% probability in Lottery A in the context of preferring lower probabilities of maximum outcomes. Instead, the justification is based on expected value and the perceived adequacy of an 80% chance. The individual's reasoning aligns with expected value maximization, not with the specific rule of preferring lotteries with lower probabilities of their maximum outcomes. There is no evidence that the decision rule was applied, even if the outcome aligns with it. The focus and justification are different.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
